{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SzKAUHLtPCtvVv2d549Vdm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AAAI 2026 conference acceptance rate statistics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 Acceptance Rate: 4,167/23,680 = 17.6% | CS Conf Stats\",\"url\":\"https://csconfstats.xoveexu.com/conferences/aaai/2026/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 Results Announced: High Score of 88887 Achieved, 17.6% Acceptance Rate for 23,000 Submissions\",\"url\":\"https://eu.36kr.com/en/p/3546803868545153\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 Accepted Papers: Outstanding Papers, Research Trends & Full Highlights\",\"url\":\"https://www.bohrium.com/en/blog/research-notes/aaai-2026-accepted-papers-highlights/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2026-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tranhungnghiep/AI-Conference-Info: Extensive acceptance rates and information of main AI conferences · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tranhungnghiep/AI-Conference-Info\"},{\"title\":\"Recently, AAAI 2026 announced the paper acceptance results. The conference is one of the top international conferences in the field of artificial intelligence. According to reports, AAAI received a total of 23,680 paper submissions in 2026, of which 4,167 papers were accepted, and the acceptance rate was only 17.6%. The paper “FastDriveVLA: Efficient End-to-End Driving via Plug-and-Play Reconstruction-based Token Pruning”, which was jointly completed by Xiaopeng Motors and the National Key Laboratory of\",\"url\":\"https://www.webull.com/news/14103351221634048\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI Acceptance Rates and Submission Stats - OpenAccept\",\"url\":\"https://openaccept.org/c/ai/aaai/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 Acceptance Rates and Submission Stats - OpenAccept\",\"url\":\"https://openaccept.org/c/ai/aaai/2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Publication - Chen's Homepage\",\"url\":\"https://allenjack.github.io/pages/publication.html\"},{\"title\":\"The 40th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the AAAI 2026 conference acceptance rate statistics:\n\n**Key Statistics:**\n\nAAAI 2026 accepted 4,167 papers out of 23,680 submissions, for an acceptance rate of 17.6%.\n\n**Additional Context:**\n\n- This 17.6% acceptance rate was the lowest in the past three years.\n- The 23,680 paper submissions set a new historical record, more than double the 12,957 valid submissions received by AAAI 2025.\n- The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 2026 (40th) was held in Singapore, Singapore.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e774981-e04a-44b5-ae6c-e426561826f8","uuid":"f7077c19-dedd-4d2d-aaae-ddf3f5942139","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:52:42.712Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"AAAI 2026 conference acceptance rate statistics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XCo8qfaTkGqasv4Pd4ncBN","content":[{"title":"AAAI 2026 Acceptance Rate: 4,167/23,680 = 17.6% | CS Conf Stats","url":"https://csconfstats.xoveexu.com/conferences/aaai/2026/"},{"title":"AAAI 2026 Results Announced: High Score of 88887 Achieved, 17.6% Acceptance Rate for 23,000 Submissions","url":"https://eu.36kr.com/en/p/3546803868545153"},{"title":"AAAI 2026 Accepted Papers: Outstanding Papers, Research Trends & Full Highlights","url":"https://www.bohrium.com/en/blog/research-notes/aaai-2026-accepted-papers-highlights/"},{"title":"AAAI 2026 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2026-statistics/"},{"title":"GitHub - tranhungnghiep/AI-Conference-Info: Extensive acceptance rates and information of main AI conferences · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/tranhungnghiep/AI-Conference-Info"},{"title":"Recently, AAAI 2026 announced the paper acceptance results. The conference is one of the top international conferences in the field of artificial intelligence. According to reports, AAAI received a total of 23,680 paper submissions in 2026, of which 4,167 papers were accepted, and the acceptance rate was only 17.6%. The paper “FastDriveVLA: Efficient End-to-End Driving via Plug-and-Play Reconstruction-based Token Pruning”, which was jointly completed by Xiaopeng Motors and the National Key Laboratory of","url":"https://www.webull.com/news/14103351221634048"},{"title":"AAAI Acceptance Rates and Submission Stats - OpenAccept","url":"https://openaccept.org/c/ai/aaai/"},{"title":"AAAI 2026 Acceptance Rates and Submission Stats - OpenAccept","url":"https://openaccept.org/c/ai/aaai/2026/"},{"title":"Publication - Chen's Homepage","url":"https://allenjack.github.io/pages/publication.html"},{"title":"The 40th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence","url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/"}]},"Based on the search results, here are the AAAI 2026 conference acceptance rate statistics:\n\n**Key Statistics:**\n\nAAAI 2026 accepted 4,167 papers out of 23,680 submissions, for an acceptance rate of 17.6%.\n\n**Additional Context:**\n\n- This 17.6% acceptance rate was the lowest in the past three years.\n- The 23,680 paper submissions set a new historical record, more than double the 12,957 valid submissions received by AAAI 2025.\n- The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 2026 (40th) was held in Singapore, Singapore."],"durationSeconds":4.17111649}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UEsfzT99ANvPi5wdu8pZGu","type":"tool_result","content":"# AAAI-26 Review Process: Details on Scoring and Evaluation\n\nBased on the provided web page content, I cannot extract specific details about review forms, scoring dimensions, rating scales, or evaluation criteria for AAAI-26 reviewers.\n\n## What the Page Contains\n\nThe document outlines the **two-phase review structure**:\n- Phase 1: Three reviewers per paper; sufficient negative reviews lead to rejection\n- Phase 2: Additional reviewers assess remaining papers without initial phase feedback\n- Author feedback window: October 7-13, 2025\n\n## What's Missing\n\nThe page does not include:\n- Numeric rating scales or point systems\n- Specific evaluation categories or dimensions\n- Detailed scoring rubrics\n- Review form templates\n\n## Related Resources\n\nThe page references an external document: \"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers\" (linked as a Google Doc), which likely contains the actual review forms and scoring criteria. Additionally, there's an \"FAQ for the AI-Assisted Peer-Review Process Pilot Program\" PDF that may address evaluation specifics.\n\nTo obtain complete information on review scoring mechanisms, you would need to access those linked documents directly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e774981-e04a-44b5-ae6c-e426561826f8","uuid":"badc411b-f6c0-48b1-affe-8a01e08ed1f5","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:52:44.619Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":199885,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# AAAI-26 Review Process: Details on Scoring and Evaluation\n\nBased on the provided web page content, I cannot extract specific details about review forms, scoring dimensions, rating scales, or evaluation criteria for AAAI-26 reviewers.\n\n## What the Page Contains\n\nThe document outlines the **two-phase review structure**:\n- Phase 1: Three reviewers per paper; sufficient negative reviews lead to rejection\n- Phase 2: Additional 