{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MDFpnvLdfR5zxTLKuuiwsK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J4dchGUbcFNFkwwLmDzJ8P","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an AAAI-level review. Your focus areas are **methodology soundness** and **experimental rigor**.\n\n## Venue: AAAI 2027 (use AAAI 2026 standards)\n- Acceptance rate: ~17.6%\n- Rating scale: 1-10 (10=award quality, 8-9=strong accept, 7=accept, 6=weak accept, 5=borderline, 4=weak reject, 3=reject, 1-2=strong reject)\n- Confidence: 1-5 (5=expert, 4=confident, 3=somewhat confident, 2=not confident, 1=no expertise)\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"ContamCal: Calibrating LLM Benchmark Scores via Contamination-Augmented Item Response Theory\"\n\nContamCal is a two-stage framework for calibrating contaminated LLM benchmark scores:\n- Stage 1: Computes per-item exposure scores by fusing 4 detection signals (embedding retrieval, Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique) via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF), a parameter-free aggregator.\n- Stage 2: Fits a contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model with per-benchmark contamination parameters γ_k and a measurement error model that propagates detection uncertainty into Bayesian credible intervals.\n\nKey results: 1.5 pp MAE on controlled SFT injection across 3 model families (Qwen, Llama, Pythia), 4 scales (0.5B-7B), 4 benchmarks (MMLU, GSM8K, ARC, HumanEval). 93% CI coverage at 95% nominal. Beats all 7 baselines including DCR (Δ=1.9pp, p=0.003). Signal survival analysis shows cliff-like degradation of logit-based signals under RL. Fisher Information identifiability analysis (AUC≥0.68, N≥35).\n\n## Experiment Design (from review_context.yaml — the FULL planned experiments)\nThe paper was designed with 12 imagined experiments:\n1. **exp-001**: Controlled SFT injection (Qwen 0.5B/1.5B/3B × 5 dosages × 3 seeds = 45 runs, 72B generates paraphrases)\n2. **exp-002**: Stage 1 signal pipeline (4 signals' per-item AUC across dosages/scales)\n3. **exp-003**: RRF aggregation ablation (RRF vs rank-avg vs cal-weighted vs single-signal vs 2-signal)\n4. **exp-004**: 144-condition simulation identifiability sweep (AUC × N × prior × exposure_type, Fisher Info)\n5. **exp-005**: Noise propagation (measurement error model vs point estimate coverage)\n6. **exp-006**: IRT calibration + 7 baselines comparison (MAE, coverage, Kendall τ, dose-response)\n7. **exp-007**: 7B scale bridging\n8. **exp-008**: Signal survival analysis (4 signals × 4 regimes AUC heatmap)\n9. **exp-009**: RL observational case study (Qwen-Instruct + DeepSeek-R1, regret analysis, near-zero γ check)\n10. **exp-012**: 72B observational analysis\n11. **exp-013**: Closed-weight 2-signal mode\n12. **exp-014**: Multi-family validation (Llama + Pythia)\n\n## What the Paper Actually Reports\nThe paper covers ALL 12 experiments across 16 tables in 10 pages. Tables 1-16 correspond to the planned experiments.\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Methodological Soundness\n- Is the contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (Eq. 3) well-motivated and correctly specified?\n- Is the measurement error model (Eq. 4) appropriate? Is σ_e properly estimated?\n- Is using RRF as the aggregator well-justified vs learned alternatives? Is the meta-circularity argument sound?\n- Are the three structural adaptations from educational IRT properly handled (independence, continuous exposure, regime-conditional)?\n- Is the local independence assumption adequately addressed (per-benchmark fitting, residual correlations ≤0.09)?\n- Are the priors appropriate (γ_k ~ HalfNormal(0.5), θ_j ~ N(0,1), a_i ~ LogNormal(0,0.5))?\n- Is the Fisher Information analysis I(γ) ∝ N·AUC²/(1-AUC²) correct? Does it truly provide the claimed theoretical grounding?\n\n### 2. Experimental Rigor\n- Is the controlled contamination injection (paraphrase-based SFT) a valid proxy for real-world contamination?\n- Are the 7 baselines comprehensive and fairly compared?\n- Are metrics appropriate (MAE, coverage, CI width, Kendall τ, dose-response R²)?\n- Is the evaluation on 4 benchmarks × 3 scales × 3 seeds sufficient for the claims?\n- Is the multi-family validation (Llama, Pythia) convincing or too shallow (only 3 dosage levels)?\n- Is the 7B scale bridging (exp-007) sufficient to claim scalability?\n- Is the RL observational case study (exp-009) convincing without ground truth?\n- Is the 72B analysis meaningful with N=1?\n- Is the near-zero γ specificity check adequate (only LiveBench)?\n- Are the statistical tests appropriate (bootstrap CI, pairwise p-values)?\n- Table 1: Only MMLU has full dosage breakdown (5/25/50/100%), other benchmarks only show 100%. Why?\n- Table 4: Many cells are missing (—). Is the identifiability analysis cherry-picked?\n- Table 13: All three RL models have identical CI width (7.8pp). Is this suspicious?\n- Table 14: Only K=5 column is filled. Where are K=3 and K=10?\n\n### 3. Reproducibility\n- Is HMC implementation described sufficiently (chains, warmup, convergence criteria)?\n- Are code/data availability discussed?\n- Can the paraphrase pipeline be reproduced?\n\n### 4. Presentation Quality\n- Are the 16 tables well-organized? Too many tables, not enough figures?\n- Is the paper within page limits? (10 pages + references for AAAI)\n- Is the writing clear and well-structured?\n\n## Output Format\nProvide your review in this exact structure:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methodology & Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\nS1. [strength]\nS2. [strength]\n...\n\n### Weaknesses\nW1. [weakness — be specific, cite table/section numbers]\nW2. [weakness]\n...\n\n### Questions for Authors\nQ1. [question]\nQ2. [question]\n...\n\n### Missing Experiments / Gaps vs Design\n[Compare paper coverage to the 12 planned experiments — what's missing or thinned?]\n\n### Minor Issues\n- [list]\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: [1-4, where 4=excellent]\n- Empirical Methodology: [1-4]\n- Clarity: [1-4]\n- Overall: [1-10 AAAI scale]\n- Confidence: [1-5]\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1334,"cache_read_input_tokens":71696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1334},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e774981-e04a-44b5-ae6c-e426561826f8","uuid":"1a35f497-c2cf-4e67-8474-c77cca0c6836"}
